---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.tsx";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · Hostbeam"
  description="What Hostbeam processes, what it never sees, and who touches what. The short version: what you beam goes from your device to your server over your own SSH. We never see it."
>
  <div class="site" id="top">
    <Nav />
    <main class="wrap" style="max-width: 720px; padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 96px">
      <p class="note">Privacy policy · last updated 9 October 2026</p>
      <h1 class="h2" style="font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px)">
        What you beam never touches us.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 20px">
        Hostbeam moves the screenshots and files you hand it from your Mac or iPhone to your own
        server over your own SSH.
        That design is the privacy policy: the file goes straight from your device to your host,
        and no Hostbeam system ever sees, stores, or relays it. This page lists the few things we
        do process, and why.
      </p>

      <section style="margin-top: 48px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">What the apps never send</h2>
        <ul style="margin: 14px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          <li>Your screenshots, photos and files. They travel over your SSH connection only.</li>
          <li>Your SSH keys, config, hostnames, or credentials.</li>
          <li>Usage analytics, crash reports, or telemetry of any kind. There is none.</li>
          <li>Your beam count. The Mac counts beams to know when to show the license reminder, and the count stays there.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section style="margin-top: 40px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">What is processed, and by whom</h2>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          <b style="color: var(--ink)">License activation and checks.</b> When you activate a license, the Mac app sends your
          license key, a device identifier (a random ID the app creates, not your Apple ID or
          advertising ID), and a device name to our licensing service,
          <a href="https://keygen.sh" style="color: var(--beam)">Keygen</a>. A licensed Mac
          re-checks the key quietly about once a day. It exists so your license works on up to three
          Macs, and for anyone without a license there is no request at all — the reminder is
          decided on your Mac. The iPhone app has no license, so it makes no such request.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          <b style="color: var(--ink)">Device permissions.</b> The iPhone app asks for camera
          access (only to scan the pairing QR from your Mac) and photo access (only to read the
          screenshot you choose to beam). Both are used on your device, in the moment; nothing
          from your camera or photo library is ever sent to us. The images and files you beam go
          to your own server, over your own SSH, and nowhere else.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          <b style="color: var(--ink)">Purchases.</b> Checkout is handled by
          <a href="https://paddle.com" style="color: var(--beam)">Paddle</a>, our merchant of
          record: legally, Paddle is the seller, and Paddle is the data controller for your
          payment and billing data, under
          <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" style="color: var(--beam)">Paddle's privacy policy</a>.
          We never see card numbers. We receive your email address and order details so we can
          create your license and email you the key
          (delivery via <a href="https://resend.com" style="color: var(--beam)">Resend</a>).
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          <b style="color: var(--ink)">Support.</b> If you email
          <a href="mailto:support@hostbeam.app" style="color: var(--beam)">support@hostbeam.app</a>,
          we keep the correspondence for as long as it's useful to help you.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          <b style="color: var(--ink)">This website.</b> Served by Cloudflare, which keeps standard
          server logs. We use
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" style="color: var(--beam)">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>:
          cookieless, no fingerprinting, no cross-site tracking. We see aggregate page views,
          never people. The site sets no cookies of its own. The home page shows a
          <a href="https://www.tinyshelf.co" style="color: var(--beam)">TinyShelf</a> badge, an
          image your browser loads from tinyshelf.co on each visit, so TinyShelf sees that request
          (your IP address and browser) as any image host would; it sets no cookie. Nothing on
          the site loads a payment provider's script: there is nothing to buy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section style="margin-top: 40px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">Your data, your call</h2>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          We keep license records for as long as your license is meant to work, which is forever,
          so they persist unless you ask otherwise. Email
          <a href="mailto:support@hostbeam.app" style="color: var(--beam)">support@hostbeam.app</a>
          to access, correct, or delete what we hold about you (your email address and license
          record), and we'll do it. Deleting a license record deactivates the license.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          Hostbeam is not directed at children, and since it has no accounts and no data
          collection, we hold no personal data about anyone, children included.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          If this policy ever changes, the date at the top changes with it, and material changes
          will be called out plainly, not buried.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          Hostbeam is an independent, developer-run product, made and operated by
          <strong>PunkABeat</strong>, a sole proprietorship. For anything about this policy or
          your data: <a href="mailto:support@hostbeam.app" style="color: var(--beam)">support@hostbeam.app</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Base>
